w: 1.~Let God a- rise, and scat- ter- èd let all his en'- mies be; And let all those that do him hate be- _ fore his pre- sence flee.
w: 2.~As smoke is driv'n, so drive thou them; as fire melts wax a- way, Be- fore God's face let wi- cked men so _ per- ish and de- cay.
w: * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
w: 4.~To God sing, to his name sing praise; ex- tol him with your voice, That rides on heav'n, by his name Jah, be- _ fore his face re- joice.
w: 5.~Be- cause the Lord a fa- ther is un- to the fa- ther- less; God is the wi- dow's judge, with- in his _ place of ho- li- ness.
w: 6.~God doth the so- li- ta- ry set in fam'- lies: and from bands The chain'd doth free; but re- bels do in- _ ha- bit parch- èd lands.
w: 7.~O God, what time thou didst go forth be- fore thy peo- ple's face; And when through the great wild- er- ness thy _ glor- ious march- ing was;
w: 8.~Then at God's pre- sence shook the earth, then drops from hea- ven fell; This Si- nai shook be- fore the Lord, the _ God of Is- ra- el.
w: 9.~O God, thou to thine he- ri- tage didst send a plent- eous rain, Where- by thou, when it wear- y was, didst _ it re- fresh a- gain.
w: 10.~Thy con- gre- ga- tion then did make their hab- i- ta- tion there: Of thine own good- ness for the poor, O _ God, thou didst pre- pare.
w: 11.~The Lord him- self did give the word, the word a- broad did spread; Great was the com- pa- ny of them the _ same who pu- blish- èd.
w: 12.~Kings of great arm- ies foil- èd were, and forced to flee a- way; And wo- men, who re- mained at home, did _ dis- tri- bute the prey.
w: 13.~Though ye have lien a- mong the pots, like doves ye shall ap- pear, Whose wings with sil- ver, and with gold whose _ fea- thers co- vered are.
w: 14.~When there th'Al- might- y scat- ter'd kings, like Sal- mon's snow 'twas white. God's hill is like to Ba- shan hill, like _ Ba- shan hill for height.
w: 15.~Why do ye leap, ye moun- tains high? this is the hill where God De- sires to dwell; yea, God in it for _ aye will make a- bode.
w: * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
w: 17.~Thou hast, O Lord, most glo- ri- ous, a- scen- ded up on high; And in tri- umph vic- tor- ious led cap- _ tive cap- ti- vi- ty:
w: 18.~Thou hast re- ceiv- èd gifts for men, for such as did re- bel; Yea, ev'n for them, that God the Lord in _ midst of them might dwell.
w: 19.~Blessed be the Lord, who is to us of our sal- va- tion God; Who dai- ly with his be- ne- fits us _ plen- teou- sly doth load.
w: 20.~He of sal- va- tion is the God, who is our God most strong; And un- to God the Lord from death the _ is- sues do be- long.
w: 21.~But sure- ly God shall wound the head of those that are his foes; The hai- ry scalp of him that still on _ in his tres- pass goes.
w: 22.~God said, My peo- ple I will bring a- gain from Ba- shan hill; Yea, from the sea's de- vou- ring depths them _ bring a- gain I will;
w: 23.~That in the blood of e- ne- mies thy foot im- brued may be, And of thy dogs dipped in the same the _ tongues thou ma- yest see.
w: 24.~Thy go- ings they have seen, O God; the steps of ma- jes- ty Of my God, and my might- y King, with- _ in the sanc- tua- ry.
w: 25.~Be- fore went sing- ers, pla- yers next on ins- tru- ments took way; And them a- mong the dam- sels were that _ did on tim- brels play.
w: 26.~With- in the cong- re- ga- ti- ons bless God with one ac- cord: From Is- r'el's foun- tain do ye bless and _ praise the might- y Lord.
w: 27.~With their prince, lit- tle Ben- ja- min, prin- ces and coun- cil there Of Ju- dah were, there Za- bu- lon's and _ Napht'- li's prin- ces were.
w: 28.~Thy God com- mands thy strength; make strong what thou wrought'st for us, Lord. For thy house at Je- ru- sa- lem kings _ shall thee gifts af- ford.
w: 29.~The spear- men's host, the mul- ti- tude of bulls, which fier- cely look, Those calves which peo- ple have forth sent, O _ Lord our God, re- buke,
w: 30.~Till ev'- ry one sub- mit him- self, and sil- ver piec- es bring: The peo- ple that de- light in war dis- _ perse, O God and King.
w: 31.~Those that be prin- ces great shall then come out of E- gypt lands; And E- thi- o- pi- a to God shall _ soon stretch out her hands.
w: 32.~O all ye king- doms of the earth, sing prais- es to this King; For he is Lord that ru- leth all, un- _ to him prais- es sing.
w: 33.~To him that rides on heav'ns of heav'ns, which he of old did found; Lo, he sends out his voice, a voice in _ might that doth a- bound.
w: 34.~Strength un- to God do ye a- scribe; fo- r his ex- cel- lency Is o- ver Is- ra- el, his strength is _ in the clouds most high.
w: 35.~Thou'rt from thy tem- ple dread- ful, Lord; Is- r'el's own God is he, Who gives his peo- ple strength and pow'r: O _ let God bless- ed be.
